{"id":"mahabharata-8-020","work":"mahabharata","part":8,"partName":"कर्णपर्व","partNameEn":"Karna Parva","unit":20,"title":"विंशतितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 20 · Yudhishthira and Duryodhana","summary":{"en":"Dhritarashtra laments the terrible sorrows he has heard, and Sanjaya tells how Duryodhana cut Yudhishthira's bow. Yudhishthira cuts down the mace hurled at him, and Bhima, taking up his gilded mace, rushes forward.","kn":"ತಾನು ಕೇಳಿದ ಅಸಹನೀಯ ದುಃಖಗಳನ್ನು ಧೃತರಾಷ್ಟ್ರ ವಿಷಾದಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ; ದುರ್ಯೋಧನ ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರನ ಬಿಲ್ಲನ್ನು ಕತ್ತರಿಸಿದುದನ್ನು ಸಂಜಯ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರ ತನ್ನ ಮೇಲೆ ಎಸೆದ ಗದೆಯನ್ನು ಕಡಿಯುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಭೀಮ ಚಿನ್ನದ ಗದೆ ಹಿಡಿದು ನುಗ್ಗುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"धृतराष्ट्र अपने सुने असहनीय दुःखों का शोक करते हैं, और संजय बताते हैं कि दुर्योधन ने युधिष्ठिर का धनुष काटा। युधिष्ठिर अपने ऊपर फेंकी गदा को काटते हैं और भीम स्वर्णमण्डित गदा लेकर दौड़ पड़ते हैं।","te":"తాను విన్న భరించలేని దుఃఖాలకు ధృతరాష్ట్రుడు విలపిస్తాడు; దుర్యోధనుడు యుధిష్ఠిరుని విల్లు ఛేదించాడని సంజయుడు చెబుతాడు. యుధిష్ఠిరుడు తనపై విసిరిన గదను నరుకుతాడు; భీముడు బంగారు గద పట్టుకుని దూకుతాడు.","ta":"தான் கேட்ட தாங்கொணாத் துயரங்களுக்குத் த்ருதராஷ்டிரன் வருந்த, துரியோதனன் யுதிஷ்டிரரின் வில்லை வெட்டியதைச் சஞ்சயன் கூறுகிறான். யுதிஷ்டிரர் தன்மீது எறியப்பட்ட கதையை வெட்ட, பீமன் பொன் கதையை ஏந்திப் பாய்கிறான்.","ml":"കേട്ട ഭയങ്കര ദുഃഖങ്ങളെക്കുറിച്ച് ധൃതരാഷ്ട്രർ വിലപിക്കുന്നു; ദുര്യോധനൻ യുധിഷ്ഠിരന്റെ വില്ല് മുറിച്ചതെങ്ങനെയെന്ന് സഞ്ജയൻ പറയുന്നു. തനിക്കെതിരെ എറിഞ്ഞ ഗദ യുധിഷ്ഠിരൻ മുറിക്കുന്നു; ഭീമൻ സ്വർണ്ണഗദയെടുത്ത് മുന്നോട്ട് കുതിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 8.20; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Jul 29 2019","sections":[{"title":"कर्णपर्व","titleEn":"Karna Parva","verses":[{"text":"धृतराष्ट्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Dhritarashtra said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"अतितीव्राणि दुःखानि दुःसहानि बहूनि च ।\nतवाहं संजयाश्रौषं पुत्राणां मम संक्षयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya, I have heard from you of many terrible griefs, hard to bear, and of the destruction of my sons."}},{"n":2,"text":"तथा तु मे कथयसे यथा युद्धं तु वर्तते ।\nन सन्ति सूत कौरव्या इति मे नैष्ठिकी मतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"From how you tell me the battle goes, my firm conviction is, charioteer, that there are no Kauravas left."}},{"n":3,"text":"दुर्योधनस्तु विरथः कृतस्तत्र महारणे ।\nधर्मपुत्रः कथं चक्रे तस्मिन्वा नृपतिः कथम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Duryodhana was left chariotless in that great battle. What did the son of Dharma do then, and what did the king Duryodhana do?"}},{"n":4,"text":"अपराह्णे कथं युद्धमभवल्लोमहर्षणम् ।\nतन्ममाचक्ष्व तत्त्वेन कुशलो ह्यसि संजय ॥","meaning":{"en":"How did the hair-raising battle go in the afternoon? Tell me truly, Sanjaya, for you are skilled."}},{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":5,"text":"संसक्तेषु च सैन्येषु युध्यमानेषु भागशः ।\nरथमन्यं समास्थाय पुत्रस्तव विशां पते ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the armies were locked and fighting in separate parts, O lord of the people, your son mounted another chariot."}},{"n":6,"text":"क्रोधेन महताविष्टः सविषो भुजगो यथा ।\nदुर्योधनस्तु दृष्ट्वा वै धर्मराजं युधिष्ठिरम् ।\nउवाच सूत त्वरितं याहि याहीति भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Filled with great anger like a venomous snake, Duryodhana saw King Yudhishthira, the king of dharma, and said to his charioteer, \"Go, go quickly, O Bharata's servant!"}},{"n":7,"text":"अत्र मां प्रापय क्षिप्रं सारथे यत्र पाण्डवः ।\nध्रियमाणेन छत्रेण राजा राजति दंशितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Take me quickly to where the Pandava is, charioteer, where the armored king shines under the parasol held over him.\""}},{"n":8,"text":"स सूतश्चोदितो राज्ञा राज्ञः स्यन्दनमुत्तमम् ।\nयुधिष्ठिरस्याभिमुखं प्रेषयामास संयुगे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Urged by the king, the charioteer drove the king's excellent chariot straight at Yudhishthira in the battle."}},{"n":9,"text":"ततो युधिष्ठिरः क्रुद्धः प्रमत्त इव सद्गवः ।\nसारथिं चोदयामास याहि यत्र सुयोधनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Yudhishthira, angry like a maddened good bull, urged his charioteer, saying, \"Go where Suyodhana is.\""}},{"n":10,"text":"तौ समाजग्मतुर्वीरौ भ्रातरौ रथसत्तमौ ।\nसमेत्य च महावीर्यौ संनद्धौ युद्धदुर्मदौ ।\nततक्षतुर्महेष्वासौ शरैरन्योन्यमाहवे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those two heroic brothers, best of chariot-warriors, met, both of great might, armored and fierce in battle, and the two great archers tore at each other with arrows in the fight."}},{"n":11,"text":"ततो दुर्योधनो राजा धर्मशीलस्य मारिष ।\nशिलाशितेन भल्लेन धनुश्चिच्छेद संयुगे ।\nतं नामृष्यत संक्रुद्धो व्यवसायं युधिष्ठिरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then King Duryodhana, O sir, cut the bow of the righteous Yudhishthira in battle with a stone-sharpened broad-headed arrow. Yudhishthira, angry, could not tolerate that act."}},{"n":12,"text":"अपविध्य धनुश्छिन्नं क्रोधसंरक्तलोचनः ।\nअन्यत्कार्मुकमादाय धर्मपुत्रश्चमूमुखे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Throwing aside the cut bow, his eyes red with anger, the son of Dharma took another bow at the front of the army."}},{"n":13,"text":"दुर्योधनस्य चिच्छेद ध्वजं कार्मुकमेव च ।\nअथान्यद्धनुरादाय प्रत्यविध्यत पाण्डवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He cut Duryodhana's standard and his bow. Duryodhana took another bow and pierced the Pandava back."}},{"n":14,"text":"तावन्योन्यं सुसंरब्धौ शरवर्षाण्यमुञ्चताम् ।\nसिंहाविव सुसंक्रुद्धौ परस्परजिगीषया ॥","meaning":{"en":"Both in fury, they let loose showers of arrows on each other, like two enraged lions each wishing to defeat the other."}},{"n":15,"text":"अन्योन्यं जघ्नतुश्चैव नर्दमानौ वृषाविव ।\nअन्योन्यं प्रेक्षमाणौ च चेरतुस्तौ महारथौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"They struck each other and roared like bulls, and those two great chariot-warriors moved about watching each other."}},{"n":16,"text":"ततः पूर्णायतोत्सृष्टैरन्योन्यं सुकृतव्रणौ ।\nविरेजतुर्महाराज पुष्पिताविव किंशुकौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, O great king, wounded by arrows drawn full and shot at each other, they shone like two flowering kimshuka trees."}},{"n":17,"text":"ततो राजन्प्रतिभयान्सिंहनादान्मुहुर्मुहुः ।\nतलयोश्च तथा शब्दान्धनुषोश्च महाहवे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, O king, they made fearful lion-roars again and again, the slap of palms and the twang of bows in that great battle,"}},{"n":18,"text":"शङ्खशब्दरवांश्चैव चक्रतुस्तौ रथोत्तमौ ।\nअन्योन्यं च महाराज पीडयां चक्रतुर्भृशम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"and the sounds of conches, those two best of chariot-warriors, and they hurt each other badly, O great king."}},{"n":19,"text":"ततो युधिष्ठिरो राजा तव पुत्रं त्रिभिः शरैः ।\nआजघानोरसि क्रुद्धो वज्रवेगो दुरासदः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then King Yudhishthira, angry, hard to approach, with the speed of a thunderbolt, struck your son in the chest with three arrows."}},{"n":20,"text":"प्रतिविव्याध तं तूर्णं तव पुत्रो महीपतिम् ।\nपञ्चभिर्निशितैर्बाणैर्हेमपुङ्खैः शिलाशितैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Your son quickly pierced the king back with five sharp, gold-feathered, stone-sharpened arrows."}},{"n":21,"text":"ततो दुर्योधनो राजा शक्तिं चिक्षेप भारत ।\nसर्वपारशवीं तीक्ष्णां महोल्काप्रतिमां तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then King Duryodhana, O Bharata, hurled a sharp spear made wholly of iron, like a great meteor."}},{"n":22,"text":"तामापतन्तीं सहसा धर्मराजः शिलाशितैः ।\nत्रिभिश्चिच्छेद सहसा तं च विव्याध सप्तभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As it came suddenly at him, the king of dharma cut it with three stone-sharpened arrows and pierced Duryodhana with seven."}},{"n":23,"text":"निपपात ततः साथ हेमदण्डा महाघना ।\nनिपतन्ती महोल्केव व्यराजच्छिखिसंनिभा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then that heavy spear with its golden shaft fell, and as it fell it shone like a great meteor, like a flame."}},{"n":24,"text":"शक्तिं विनिहतां दृष्ट्वा पुत्रस्तव विशां पते ।\nनवभिर्निशितैर्भल्लैर्निजघान युधिष्ठिरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the spear destroyed, your son, O lord of the people, struck Yudhishthira with nine sharp broad-headed arrows."}},{"n":25,"text":"सोऽतिविद्धो बलवतामग्रणीः शत्रुतापनः ।\nदुर्योधनं समुद्दिश्य बाणं जग्राह सत्वरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Badly pierced, the foremost of the strong, the tormentor of foes, quickly took an arrow aimed at Duryodhana."}},{"n":26,"text":"समाधत्त च तं बाणं धनुष्युग्रं महाबलः ।\nचिक्षेप च ततो राजा राज्ञः क्रुद्धः पराक्रमी ॥","meaning":{"en":"The mighty one fitted that fierce arrow to his bow, and then the angry, valiant king shot it at the king."}},{"n":27,"text":"स तु बाणः समासाद्य तव पुत्रं महारथम् ।\nव्यमोहयत राजानं धरणीं च जगाम ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"That arrow reached your son, the great chariot-warrior, bewildered the king and then went into the ground."}},{"n":28,"text":"ततो दुर्योधनः क्रुद्धो गदामुद्यम्य वेगितः ।\nविधित्सुः कलहस्यान्तमभिदुद्राव पाण्डवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Duryodhana, angry and swift, raised his mace and rushed at the Pandava, wishing to end the quarrel."}},{"n":29,"text":"तमालक्ष्योद्यतगदं दण्डहस्तमिवान्तकम् ।\nधर्मराजो महाशक्तिं प्राहिणोत्तव सूनवे ।\nदीप्यमानां महावेगां महोल्कां ज्वलितामिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing him with raised mace, like Death with his rod, the king of dharma hurled a great spear at your son, blazing, very swift, like a flaming great meteor."}},{"n":30,"text":"रथस्थः स तया विद्धो वर्म भित्त्वा महाहवे ।\nभृशं संविग्नहृदयः पपात च मुमोह च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Struck by it as he stood in his chariot, it broke his armor in that great battle, and, his heart badly shaken, he fell and fainted."}},{"n":31,"text":"ततस्त्वरितमागत्य कृतवर्मा तवात्मजम् ।\nप्रत्यपद्यत राजानं मग्नं वै व्यसनार्णवे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Kritavarman came quickly to your son, the king, who was sunk in an ocean of disaster, and took care of him."}},{"n":32,"text":"भीमोऽपि महतीं गृह्य गदां हेमपरिष्कृताम् ।\nअभिदुद्राव वेगेन कृतवर्माणमाहवे ।\nएवं तदभवद्युद्धं त्वदीयानां परैः सह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhima too, taking a great gold-decked mace, rushed swiftly at Kritavarman in the battle. Thus that battle of your men with the enemy went on."}}]}]}